Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:10:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(auth): keep removed pool rows deleted across stale
 runtime flushes [daveey]

Cause: the locked pool writer retained concurrent disk additions but treated all
incoming rows as additions, including rows removed since a runtime loaded them.
Use the existing per-id generation bases to distinguish new rows from deleted
known rows while merging against the locked disk snapshot. Reconcile removed
known rows and current selection in memory so a second flush cannot reinsert them.
Keep ephemeral seeded rows without a persisted baseline for borrowed singletons.

Proof: cross-process removal followed by stale cooldown persistence fails five
regressions on the original code, then passes. All 35 pool/auth files pass (282
tests). Removing the disk filter kills five tests; removing memory reconciliation
kills four. scripts/check --base origin/main: 21 checks pass.

Implemented-by: gpt-6.1-sol (OpenAI)
